WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Four small French verbs
run your weekend plans:

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.320
«pouvoir», «vouloir», «devoir», «savoir».

3
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.710
Can, want, must, know how to.

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.750
But watch one of them change shape.

5
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.950
«Je peux». Then «nous pouvons».

6
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.490
Same verb, a different stem.

7
00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:19.610
And each of these verbs can pull a second

8
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.230
verb along behind it.

9
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.400
So in 'I want to go out',

10
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.520
which verb does French change?

11
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.250
And where does the little word 'to' go?

12
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.970
In this mission, you'll watch
two verbs become one engine,

13
00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.710
and find the boot hiding in the verb grid.

14
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.340
Then you'll build the
forms yourself in the lab,

15
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.760
and sort verbs into three lanes.

16
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.120
Your mission: crack the
two-verb pattern and find out

17
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.430
where the 'to' goes.
